<DocLayout
  title="Provenance limits"
  description="Limits of Image Identifier evidence — conflicts, incomplete checks, and why results are not certification."
  updated="2026-10-14"
>
  <p>
    Image Identifier reconciles independent checks into evidence labels. It preserves conflicts
    instead of inventing a single “authentic” or “fake” stamp.
  </p>

  <h2>Hard limits</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>No guarantee of real vs fake.</li>
    <li>No legal or journalistic certification.</li>
    <li>Not every generator, camera, or editor leaves detectable traces.</li>
    <li>Optional statistical scoring is incomplete and error-prone.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Conflicting evidence</h2>
  <p>
    Example: camera-related details can appear alongside generation-related clues. The summary should
    show conflict rather than picking a winner. Inspect each tab for the raw signals.
  </p>

  <h2>Incomplete analysis</h2>
  <p>
    If one check fails, others may still succeed. “Analysis incomplete” means at least one path did
    not finish — not that the image is suspicious by itself.
  </p>

  <p>
    See also <a href="/methodology/">Limits (summary)</a> and the
    <a href="/guides/">full guide index</a>.
  </p>
</DocLayout>
